    <md:uuid>692102b2-36bc-43fc-83f1-b703f7ed4675</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 3, choose an equivalent equation.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="b52a52a3-95d8-4b74-8c07-2cb024e1c0f1"><problem><para>
      <para>1. Which equation is equivalent to \(3x + 6 = 4x + 7\)?</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(7x=1\)</para><para>\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para><para>\(9x=4x+7\)</para><para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para><para>\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(3x-1=4x\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
